        "y1": 0.3299586789276045
      },
      "text": "(iii-3) If µ f > 0 , then E [ ‖ ˆ x η -x ∗ ‖ 2 ] ≤ 2 ηµ f Err η .",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11764705882352941,
        "y0": 0.34811293472222216,
        "x1": 0.884831866050196,
        "y1": 0.4018467664141414
      },
      "text": "Proof. (i-1) In view of the definition of Err η and f η , we have E [ h (ˆ x η ) + ηf (ˆ x η )] -f ∗ η ≤ Err η . Also, from the definition of f ∗ η , we have f ∗ η ≤ f η ( x ∗ ) = h ∗ + ηf ∗ . From the preceding two relations, we obtain",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "formula",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.3403333333333333,
        "y0": 0.4126937428030303,
        "x1": 0.8844389672875818,
        "y1": 0.4322116654040403
      },
      "text": "",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11764705882352941,
        "y0": 0.4430586417929293,
        "x1": 0.882841457339608,
        "y1": 0.49679247348484845
      },
      "text": "By invoking Assumption 1, we have E [ f (ˆ x η )] > -∞ . Therefore, there exists some M > 0 such that f ∗ -E [ f (ˆ x η )] < M . As a result, we obtain E [ h (ˆ x η )] -h ∗ ≤ Err η + ηM . From ˆ x η ∈ X , we also have E [ h (ˆ x η )] -h ∗ ≥ 0. This completes the proof of (i-1).",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11556209150326797,
        "y0": 0.4943818741161617,
        "x1": 0.8848360300039539,
        "y1": 0.5310071199494949
      },
      "text": "(i-2) The upper bound holds in view of (2) and that E [ h (ˆ x η )] -h ∗ ≥ 0. To show the lower bound, from the convexity of f , we may write",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "formula",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.2800669934640523,
        "y0": 0.5418553589646464,
        "x1": 0.7218865163071897,
        "y1": 0.5640797972222221
      },
      "text": "",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11700490196078431,
        "y0": 0.5722202579545455,
        "x1": 0.8858118520584968,
        "y1": 0.6088455037878787
      },
      "text": "where the expectation is taken with respect to the random variables generated in the method M . Note that ∇ f ( x ∗ ) ⊤ E [(ˆ x η -x ∗ )] is not necessarily nonnegative. We may write",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "formula",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.19624346405228757,
        "y0": 0.6196937428030302,
        "x1": 0.8057100457189543,
        "y1": 0.6426783758973016
      },
      "text": "",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11764705882352941,
        "y0": 0.6549955104797981,
        "x1": 0.733325686601307,
        "y1": 0.6779801435740695
      },
      "text": "In view of Π X ∗ h [ˆ x η ] ∈ X ∗ h , we have ∇ f ( x ∗ ) ⊤ E [( Π X ∗ h [ˆ x η ] -x ∗ )] ≥ 0. We obtain",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "formula",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.2535179738562091,
        "y0": 0.6921533387626262,
        "x1": 0.747621755114379,
        "y1": 0.7151392344831601
      },
      "text": "",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11764705882352941,
        "y0": 0.724035914520202,
        "x1": 0.5173051458823527,
        "y1": 0.7435538371212121
      },
      "text": "Invoking the Cauchy-Schwarz inequality, we obtain",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "formula",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.24711111111111111,
        "y0": 0.7559942478535353,
        "x1": 0.7548423986601309,
        "y1": 0.7793959090909093
      },
      "text": "",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.1176470588235296,
        "y0": 0.7878768236111112,
        "x1": 0.4528273737908496,
        "y1": 0.8073947462121213
      },
      "text": "Invoking the Jensen's inequality, we obtain",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "formula",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.2471111111111113,
        "y0": 0.8198351569444444,
        "x1": 0.7548423986601309,
        "y1": 0.8432368181818182
      },
      "text": "",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11556209150326818,
        "y0": 0.8569929852272729,
        "x1": 0.7885840158660128,
        "y1": 0.8959780795454547
      },
      "text": "Noting that E [dist(ˆ x η , X ∗ h )] = E [∥ ∥ ∥ ˆ x η -Π X ∗ h [ˆ x η ] ∥ ∥ ∥ ] , we obtain the lower bound in (i-2). (i-3) This result follows directly from (i-2).",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.11556209150326818,
        "y0": 0.8935674801767678,
        "x1": 0.4006282827124183,
        "y1": 0.9130854027777779
      },
      "text": "(ii-1) This result is identical to (i-1).",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.4385767973856209,
        "y0": 0.14692613131313131,
        "x1": 0.44829847176470583,
        "y1": 0.15497671717171724
      },
      "text": "(",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
